{
  "switch": "--enable-unsafe-swiftshader",
  "playwrightVersion": "1.62.1",
  "finding": "Playwright 1.62 pushes --enable-unsafe-swiftshader on every platform; until 1.62 the push was guarded by os.platform() === 'darwin'. The switch lets Chrome fall back to the SwiftShader software renderer when no usable GPU is present, which a hand-started Chrome refuses to do. On this GPU-less host a headful Playwright browser therefore had WebGL where the reference had none. Suppressing the switch through ignoreDefaultArgs restores parity headful and changes nothing headless, because headless Chrome enables SwiftShader itself.",
